  "narrative": {
    "intro": "QTC Medical Services obligated $2.3B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. QTC Medical Services won 41 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $55.1M. QTC Medical Services' obligations are down 21.7% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer, obligating $2.2B to QTC Medical Services in FY2026 to date. Other notable buyers include the Department of Defense at $29.2M, the Department of Homeland Security at $2M, the Department of Justice at $1.1M, and the Department of the Interior at $284K. Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) is the largest market for QTC Medical Services at $2.2B, followed by Offices of Physicians, Mental Health Specialists at $29.2M. Historical obligations show FY21 $1B, FY22 $935M, FY23 $1.2B, FY24 $1.9B, and FY25 $2.9B. Current-year totals are partial because the period is FY2026 to date, and the note clarifies that totals are contract obligations except where tables show total contract values.",
    "sections": [
